 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An iodothyronine compound having iodo substituents at the 3-, 3&apos;- and 5-positions. Although some is produced in the thyroid, most of the 3,3&apos;,5-triiodo-L-thyronine in the body is generated by mono-deiodination of L-thyroxine in the peripheral tissues. Its metabolic activity is about 3 to 5 times that of L-thyroxine. The sodium salt is used in the treatment of hypothyroidism.</bp:comment>
