 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Maleylacetoacetate isomerase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_GSTZ1_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_O43708" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAAI_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.5.1.18</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GSTZ1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GSTZ1-1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glutathione S-transferase zeta 1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAAI</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5.2.1.2</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_O43708_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_1FW1_see-also</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_04785_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_2954</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference106335</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Bifunctional enzyme showing minimal glutathione-conjugating activity with ethacrynic acid and 7-chloro-4-nitrobenz-2-oxa-1,3-diazole and maleylacetoacetate isomeraseactivity. Has also low glutathione peroxidase activity with T-butyl and cumene hydroperoxides. Is able to catalyze theglutathione dependent oxygenation of dichloroacetic acid toglyoxylic acid. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10739172}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=4-maleylacetoacetate = 4-fumarylacetoacetate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:14817, ChEBI:CHEBI:17105, ChEBI:CHEBI:18034;EC=5.2.1.2; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10739172};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=glutathione + RX = a halide anion + an S-substitutedglutathione + H(+); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:16437, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:16042, ChEBI:CHEBI:17792, ChEBI:CHEBI:57925,ChEBI:CHEBI:90779; EC=2.5.1.18;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10739172};COFACTOR:Name=glutathione; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:57925;Note=Glutathione is required for the MAAI activity.;PATHWAY: Amino-acid degradation; L-phenylalanine degradation;acetoacetate and fumarate from L-phenylalanine: step 5/6.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11327815}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm {ECO:0000250}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=3;Name=1;IsoId=O43708-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=O43708-2; Sequence=VSP_039862;Name=3;IsoId=O43708-3; Sequence=VSP_047392;Note=Gene prediction based on EST data.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Mostly expressed in liver followed by kidney,skeletal muscle and brain. Also expressed in melanocytes,synovium, placenta, breast and fetal liver and heart.DISEASE: Maleylacetoacetate isomerase deficiency (MAAID)[MIM:617596]: An autosomal recessive inborn error of metabolismcharacterized by mild elevations in succinylacetone in blood andurine, usually identified by newborn screening. Liver function andcoagulation are normal. MAAID is a benign disorder.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:27876694}. Note=The disease is caused bymutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the GST superfamily. Zeta family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=NIEHS-SNPs;URL=&quot;http://egp.gs.washington.edu/data/gstz1/&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/A0A0C4DFM0</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/uniprot/A6NED0</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAAI_HUMAN Reviewed; 216 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_665877</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

