<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P46952">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-hydroxyanthranilate 3,4-dioxygenase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P46952" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_HAAO_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3HAO_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.13.11.6</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-hydroxyanthranilate oxygenase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-hydroxyanthranilic acid dioxygenase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HAAO</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3-HAO</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HAD</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">h3HAO</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_23498</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_036337</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_23498</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference127053</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P46952_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3HAO_HUMAN Reviewed; 286 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_05158_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the oxidative ring opening of 3-hydroxyanthranilate to 2-amino-3-carboxymuconate semialdehyde,which spontaneously cyclizes to quinolinate. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28792876,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7514594}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=3-hydroxyanthranilate + O2 = (2Z,4Z)-2-amino-3-carboxymuconate 6-semialdehyde; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:17953,ChEBI:CHEBI:15379, ChEBI:CHEBI:36559, ChEBI:CHEBI:77612;EC=1.13.11.6; Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28792876, ECO:0000269|PubMed:7514594};COFACTOR:Name=Fe(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29033;Evidence={ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28375145, ECO:0000269|PubMed:7514594};PATHWAY: Cofactor biosynthesis; NAD(+) biosynthesis; quinolinatefrom L-kynurenine: step 3/3. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28792876}.SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28375145, ECO:0000269|Ref.10}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm, cytosol{ECO:0000305|PubMed:7514594}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=P46952-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P46952-2; Sequence=VSP_036239;DISEASE: Vertebral, cardiac, renal, and limb defects syndrome 1(VCRL1) [MIM:617660]: An autosomal recessive congenitalmalformation syndrome characterized by vertebral segmentationabnormalities, congenital cardiac defects, renal defects, anddistal mild limb defects. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28792876}. Note=Thedisease is caused by mutations affecting the gene represented inthis entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the 3-HAO family. {ECO:0000255|HAMAP-Rule:MF_03019}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

